  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRG: Democratic Elections and Political Processes (DEPP) Leader with Associate (LWA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Development, Democracy, and Innovation (D):  With FY 2022 funds, the Democratic Elections and Political Processes (DEPP) Leader with Associate (LWA) Awards will support three priority areas of programming under the Leader award: (a) rapid and flexible response (RFR) activities address unanticipated needs, emerging opportunities and critical gaps in programming. Rapid response activities can enable a quick start up of activities in a time sensitive and rapidly evolving situation, (b) targeted interventions or pilot programs to encourage innovations, creative solutions and/or target distinct issues or solve particular problems including in countries not undergoing transitions, (c) technical leadership activities to conduct innovative research resulting in the development of widely disseminated practical user-friendly guides, tools, and training publications in the field of elections and political transitions. This may include applied research, knowledge management activities, and evaluation of programs and experiences across regions to identify best practices and lessons learned. Technical leadership may also include convening events to share and disseminate lessons learned throughout the development community and among relevant stakeholders. The LWAs field-oriented approach aligns with the Development, Democracy, and Innovation Bureau&apos;s focus on serving Missions.</narrative>
  </description>
